.TH CHARANIMATION 1
.SH NAME
charanimation \- an animated font glyph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/charanimation
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I CharAnimation
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/CharAnimation.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A TempleOS font is 256 glyphs of eight bytes and
.B text.font
is a pointer at it, so copying the font, repointing that global and
rewriting the eight bytes of the space character makes every space
already on the screen ripple without anything being redrawn.  The four
masks are one diagonal shifted a pixel at a time, which is what makes it
flow rather than flicker.
.PP
There is no shared font to repoint here, so this port draws the wave
glyph itself wherever a space falls in its own text.  The original
changes every space on the display.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/charanimation.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
